seg-7826929c89f6 = A catalogue test has a dotted id, <c1/> (for example <c2/>: type { "1" } jamming, group { "2" }, test { "5" }). The plan lists, per test area and time slot, which id is scheduled. Types { "1" } (jamming), { "2" } (spoofing) and { "3" } (meaconing) transmit; type { "0" } (briefings, grace period, booking and ad hoc slots) does not and is skipped. Plan times are local wall-clock; <c3/> (default { "2" }, CEST) says how far they are from UTC. The plan files carry a test-contact field with a person's name: it is never read, and nothing derived from it is written.

