seg-84a34f13e93b = A test is scorable only if it starts at least <c1/> after the log began; a log with an earlier test is flagged <c2/> (the baseline may have been formed under interference). <b>False alarms</b> are alarming post-calibration epochs outside every slot extended by <c3/> ({ "60" } s) before and after (or after the recovery point), counted as epochs and as runs, with runs per hour of clean time. With <c4/> and <c5/> the run is written as a signed evidence pack (<c6/>): the scorecard and the imported schedule sit inside <c7/>, so inside the hash chain and the signature. A pack is a technical record, not a legal opinion.

